# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts Tomcat (catalina.sh start) in the background and
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * Tomcat is ALREADY RUNNING with the vulnerable config when the agent
#     starts, which makes the "fixed the config but never restarted" case
#     detectable (the live server still serves readonly=false);
#   * PID 1 is `sleep infinity`, so restarting Tomcat cannot kill the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RESTART Tomcat, not merely edit the
# config — the running server keeps the old (vulnerable) config until restart.
